  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multisectoral Emergency Assistance for Vulnerable Displaced Populations in Northwest Syria (NWS)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM proposes to provide humanitarian assistance to the most vulnerable populations inside northwest Syria (NWS) and support crisis-affected groups with emergency winterization, Water, Sanitation, and Hygiene (WASH), and health services. Through these activities, IOM plans to support 31,550 beneficiaries (7,972 men, 8,861 women, 7,366 boys, 7,351 girls), including internally displaced persons (IDPs) and host community members.</narrative>
  </description>
